use pixi 0.81.0 python

# PGHOST, PGPORT, PGUSER, PGDATABASE and UVICORN_PORT. Nothing else loads them: the app
# reads the environment and opens no file of its own, poe declares no `envfile`, and in CI
# setup-direnv forwards whatever this line produces.
dotenv_if_exists backend/.env

# IMAGE_PREFIX, IMAGE_VERSION, API_BASE_URL, CURRENCY_DATA_DIR and EXPENSE_DATA_DIR -
# every name stack/compose.yaml interpolates, which is what release.yml requires of a
# compose directory. Loaded here rather than left to compose's own auto-loading of the
# .env beside a compose file, so that every .env in this repository reaches a shell by one
# mechanism. Compose auto-loads it as well, from the same file, so the two cannot
# disagree, and `poe load-expenses` reads EXPENSE_DATA_DIR from this line.
dotenv_if_exists stack/.env

# Per-machine overrides, layered on top of the defaults above so a value that names a
# place rather than the project - EXPENSE_DATA_DIR - can be redirected without editing a
# tracked file. Absent on most machines, which is why this is `_if_exists`. Matches the
# `.env*` rule in .gitignore, and is not among the three names negated back in there.
dotenv_if_exists backend/.env.local
